{"title":"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Michael picks three <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/a/74acc0662397b0c5728cedbd6881ea89e9c9c1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$different$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"82\" height=\"18\" /> digits from the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2303664ac9f0965e10eace539666415794b052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> and forms a mixed number by placing the digits in the spaces of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31e69f4c3a73052a14589794a898dd73c3a2e5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Box \\frac{\\Box}{\\Box}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"33\" height=\"36\" />. The fractional part of the mixed number must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/f/b5f0635ac5f47199efdd6154ab6f1f33af9d44ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />). What is the difference between the largest and smallest possible mixed number that can be formed?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5c2e8ce698ab7f319f7e14b33880bd4c482f701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 4 \\frac{3}{5} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 4 \\frac{9}{20} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 4 \\frac{3}{10} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 4 \\frac{4}{15} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 4 \\frac{7}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"490\" height=\"38\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the largest mixed number, we need to pick the largest number from the set for the whole part and then making the fraction as big as possible.\n</p><p>Using this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1dd3d51d73986f7af03242f480d39b68ef35cd5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> as the largest possible mixed number.\n</p><p>Next, to find the smallest number, we need to minimize the whole part by picking the smallest number from the set and then making the fraction as small as possible.\n</p><p>Using this, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d23a726134134643fb62ef22914bebf53f84bfcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\frac{2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> as the smallest possible mixed number.\n</p><p>Subtracting these, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed8db63560fa16ce78f7ce9f1ccadb7b7ba7c8b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\frac{3}{4} - 1 \\frac{2}{5} = 4 + \\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{2}{5} = 4 + \\frac{3 \\times 5}{4 \\times 5} - \\frac{2 \\times 4}{5 \\times 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"339\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8bb68fa33483515dff7bbd4aadbeeb1599a7ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=4 + \\frac{15 - 8}{20} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 4 \\frac{7}{20}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"206\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/P